From 2fcd4644be64842cca69c9aa4f18b8b1e33ea4a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 18:18:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 15/20] qwen3_5 HIP: every cache slot names an execution, not a
 layer

A looped checkpoint runs a layer more than once, and each visit owns
its state: 14 attention slots where the checkpoint has 8 attention
layers, 42 delta slots where it has 24. The pages pool, a stream's
caches, the rounds' plan buffer and their snapshots, the keep's
replay and the memory budgets now all count and index a forward's
executions (loop_plan.steps of the shared Spec), with the kind of
each slot read through the plan's physical().

A model without a loop keeps its exact layout: steps equals layers
and every index is the one it was.
